# Owner standards

Owner: coolman1984. Users are dispatchers, GA staff, finance, and drivers. They are not technical. The office program is offline-first Windows software for a small Egyptian transport office.

Read `LAUNCH_SCOPE.md` before `CLAUDE.md`, `docs/EXECUTION_PLAN.md`, and `TASKS.md`. Launch gates L1–L6 outrank the old unchecked backlog. A newer explicit instruction from the owner wins; then update the docs in the same change. Do not start a deferred feature only because its box is empty. Do not overwrite another agent's branch, and do not force-push.

## Communication

- Reports to the owner are short, clear Egyptian Arabic, with no jargon. Use an Arabic word when one exists (إكسل، الشاشة، الرابط).
- Order: **الخلاصة** (one or two lines) → **اللي اتعمل** → **محتاج منك** (every open decision, with the default in brackets) → **الخطوة الجاية**. Ask every open question in one message. Say plainly what failed or was skipped, and why.
- Do not paste code or long file lists. Name at most the one to three files that matter.
- Code, commit messages, and code comments stay in English. Commit subject is imperative; the body says why.
- Help texts (`gd.` `sit.` `path.` `help.` `tour.` `slide.`) are simple formal Arabic (العربية الميسّرة). `tests/test_guide_gate.py` is the release lint. Excel export headers stay the original English, including `Depatment`, `Strat KM`, and the leading space on ` KM`.

## Product

Ship work that looks finished: polished, professional, elegant, and modern, with enough depth that a screen is not an empty form. A bare-minimum page is not done. Scope still follows `LAUNCH_SCOPE.md`: the first paid pilot is the office journey (trips, review, monthly report, backup/restore). Extras are a later release or a separately accepted add-on. Quality of what is in scope is not optional. Do not waive a data or security failure as "not perfect".

Design lives in `docs/DESIGN.md`:

- One clear action per screen, plain words, empty states that say the next step. Calm control room, not a marketing site. Light theme has depth (canvas, card, raised), not a flat white page. Motion explains; honor reduced motion and the motion switch. Colours come from tokens. Green, amber, and red are trust colours only.
- Personalization is part of the product: font size S / M / L / XL, density, motion on/off, language, and the bundled fonts (IBM Plex Sans, IBM Plex Sans Arabic, Cairo, Tajawal, Noto Kufi Arabic, and the system font). Themes: Daylight, Night Road, Asphalt, Highway, High contrast. A screen is checked in both languages, both main themes, and at XL.
- Arabic RTL is first-class. Every UI string is a key in `js/i18n/en.js` and `js/i18n/ar.js`. Layout uses logical CSS (`margin-inline-start`, `inset-inline-end`), never `left` / `right`. Directional icons mirror. Kilometres, plates, money, and trip numbers stay LTR inside RTL (`<bdi>` or `dir="ltr"`).
- Offline-first. The office program runs without the internet. The office PC is not reachable from the public internet. Driver links, photos, and the mailbox are a later lane; queued facts on the phone are not deleted before the office has them.
- Prefer simple, low-cost, free-tier tools. Office runtime is the Python standard library only. The driver page and gateway are plain JS with no runtime packages. OFL fonts are bundled. Cloudflare stays on the free worker path unless the owner accepts a paid service. Test-only tools (Playwright, wrangler) are allowed. Do not run `playwright install`; use the browser already on the machine.
- Company name, logo, and legal text live only in `config.json` (`brand.*`, `form.legal_text`), never in code.
- Empty, loading (skeleton), and error states exist. The error says what happened and how to fix it. A save looks successful only after it is saved.

## Safety — stop and ask

- Never put passwords, keys, tokens, or other secrets in the repository, logs, tests, Excel, error text, or the activity log. Store hashes. The gateway keys cards by token hash. This repository is public: never commit the owner's workbook, paper form, photos, or real names. Those files belong in `samples/private/` (gitignored).
- Never delete customer data. Soft delete only. Restore is a new change. Never roll back history. Never copy a database file from one PC to another. Record ids are random. Trip numbers carry the PC letter.
- Get the owner's approval before anything that changes money (rates, repricing, settlement), deletes or purges records beyond the normal recycle bin, or publishes a release. Do not bump `server/version.py` onto `main`. A new version on `main` publishes `TripOrders-Setup-<version>.exe`. Preparing a candidate is not publishing it.
- A link never carries administrator rights. Every write is checked on the server and audited. A new current rate must not reprice a past trip. Do not contact customers. Do not open the office PC to the internet.

## Workflow

- Work on a branch. Open a pull request. Never merge it yourself. Never push to `main`. Never force-push. Never publish a release. Wait for the owner, and for automatic reviews, before a merge.
- Keep each pull request to one change.
- Run the full suite before pushing and report the result (pass, fail, or skipped, with the reason):
  - `cd gateway && node --test --no-warnings test/gateway.test.js`
  - `cd tests && python -m unittest test_unit test_convergence test_design test_domain test_trips_api test_xlsx test_excel_io test_word_io test_formats test_gateway_client test_permissions test_pricing test_network test_backup test_time test_import_errors test_multinode test_access_gate test_errors test_guide test_guide_gate test_assist test_e2e_browser test_e2e_driver test_e2e_link_ui test_e2e_guide test_release_files test_crypto`
- Nothing is pushed red. Do not edit `server/` or `js/` while the multi-PC or browser tests are running. Kill test servers by PID, not `pkill -f`.
- In the same pull request, when the change touches them: `DEVELOPMENT_HISTORY.md` (newest first: what, why, mistakes, lessons, gate, checks, skips, next step), `TASKS.md` (tick the task; never delete a line; strike through with a reason), guides, and `docs/RELEASE_NOTES.md` for anything the user can see. Add a reusable idea to `IDEAS.md` once that file exists.
- A bug fix includes a regression test that fails on the old code. A larger change gets an independent review; fix every verified finding. Confirm a review claim with a failing test before changing behavior.

## Review

- Validate inputs on the server: dates, kilometres, times, status, and money. Refuse impossible values. Cover the edges: empty database, retry, two PCs, offline, cancelled and closed trips, overlapping trips, and a missing rate.
- New UI text is a key in both `js/i18n/ar.js` and `js/i18n/en.js`. A new permission, page, or profile has its words in both dictionaries (`perm.*`, `permgroup.*`, `prof.*`). Help text passes `tests/test_guide_gate.py`.
- Re-read the diff for RTL, the dark theme, offline use, and an empty database. No literal words in templates. No physical `left` / `right`. No colours outside tokens.
- Do not regress the Windows installer. `tools/build_windows.py`, `installer/trip-orders.iss`, and the `windows-installer` job (build, start, serve pages) must keep working. Installed data stays in `%ProgramData%\TripOrders`. An update replaces the program only and respects an existing `config.json`.
